spans.s:
(often confounded with √ स्यन्द्) cl. 1. Ā. (Dhātup. ii, 13) स्पन्दते (rarely ˚ति; only in pres. base and inf. स्पन्दितुम्; Gr. also pf. पस्पन्दे; fut. स्पन्दिता, स्पन्दिष्यते; aor. अस्पन्दिष्ट),
to quiver, throb, twitch, tremble, vibrate, quake, palpitate, throb with life, quicken (as a child in the womb), PārGṛ.; Car.; MBh. &c.;
to kick (as an animal), Br.; ĀśvŚr.;
to make any quick movement, move, be active, Hariv.;
to flash into life, come suddenly to life, BhP. :
Caus. स्पन्दयति (aor. अपस्पन्दत्), to cause to quiver or shake, MBh.;
to move (trans.), ĀśvŚr. :
Desid. पिस्पन्दिषते Gr.:
Intens., See पनिष्पद॑.
